  INSERT INTO vr_measure_issues (measure_id, issue_key, weight, is_primary, support_meaning, rationale, source_url) VALUES
    (m_h_r_2056, 'border_security', 75, true, 'yea_supports', 'The Act''s whole mechanism is the state and local end of federal immigration enforcement: it forbids the District from adopting a law, policy or practice that stops its entities from sending, receiving, maintaining or exchanging citizenship or immigration status information, and from declining lawful federal requests. border_security''s written scope in issue-scope.js names, as what is IN, ''the state and local cooperation that feeds the federal system'' -- this Act is that clause and almost nothing else. Weight 75 rather than 100 because the key''s scope also covers the physical border and the entry apparatus, which this Act does not touch, and because the carve-out for witnesses and victims of crime is a real limit on the mandate rather than a recital. A yea compelled the cooperation.', 'https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/BILLS-119hr2056eh/html/BILLS-119hr2056eh.htm')
  INSERT INTO vr_measure_issues (measure_id, issue_key, weight, is_primary, support_meaning, rationale, source_url) VALUES
    (m_h_r_2056, 'deportations', 70, false, 'yea_supports', 'The second operative limb reaches detainers and release notification -- the District may not decline a lawful request to hold or to notify before release -- and that is the hand-off by which a person in local custody enters removal proceedings. deportations'' written scope names ''mandatory custody and removal -- who the executive must detain and place in removal proceedings''. This Act does not itself order a removal, which is why it is filed at 70 and secondary: it removes the local discretion that currently interrupts the chain. The CRS summary confirms the clause; the engrossed text was read for it rather than the summary alone.', 'https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/BILLS-119hr2056eh/html/BILLS-119hr2056eh.htm')
  INSERT INTO vr_measure_issues (measure_id, issue_key, weight, is_primary, support_meaning, rationale, source_url) VALUES
    (m_h_r_4922, 'tough_on_crime', 90, true, 'yea_supports', 'Two of the Act''s three operative limbs are inside tough_on_crime''s written enumeration verbatim. The key is IN for ''how long a person or a case stays in the system: offence elements, offence levels, mandatory minimums, sentencing enhancements, and juvenile adjustment and expungement eligibility''. Cutting the youth offender ceiling from 24 to 18 is juvenile adjustment eligibility; repealing the authority to sentence a youth offender below the mandatory minimum is a mandatory minimum. The key''s pole reads ''Advanced = the vote increased exposure to punishment or time in custody'', and both limbs do that on their face. Weight 90 rather than 100 because the third operative limb -- the Home Rule Act amendment freezing the Council''s sentencing authority -- is a federal-local authority question this wave refuses to file at all, and the weight is where that remainder is recorded rather than in a second row on a key that takes no roll calls.', 'https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/BILLS-119hr4922eh/html/BILLS-119hr4922eh.htm')
  INSERT INTO vr_measure_issues (measure_id, issue_key, weight, is_primary, support_meaning, rationale, source_url) VALUES
    (m_h_r_5140, 'tough_on_crime', 100, true, 'yea_supports', 'One operative provision and nothing else: the age at which a minor charged with the enumerated violent offences leaves family court for adult court drops to 14. tough_on_crime''s written scope is IN for ''juvenile adjustment'' eligibility by name, and its pole reads ''Advanced = the vote increased exposure to punishment or time in custody'' -- adult court is the greater exposure, which is the entire point of the change. There is no remainder to record in a weight, so the weight is 100.', 'https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/BILLS-119hr5140eh/html/BILLS-119hr5140eh.htm')
  INSERT INTO vr_measure_issues (measure_id, issue_key, weight, is_primary, support_meaning, rationale, source_url) VALUES
    (m_h_r_5214, 'tough_on_crime', 90, true, 'yea_supports', 'This one is argued on the key''s IN headline and its pole line rather than on the enumeration, because bail is not in the enumeration and pretending otherwise would be the keyword reasoning rule 41 forbids. The headline is ''Criminal exposure and time served -- what is an offence, at what level, and how long a person or a case stays in the system'', and the pole is ''Advanced = the vote increased exposure to punishment or time in custody''. The Act makes detention mandatory for two classes of charge where a judge now decides, and conditions release on cash for a third. Time in custody before trial is time in custody, and how long a case stays in the system is the headline in terms. Weight 90 because the mechanism is pretrial process rather than an offence level or a sentence, and the enumeration reaches the latter.', 'https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/BILLS-119hr5214eh/html/BILLS-119hr5214eh.htm')
  INSERT INTO vr_measure_issues (measure_id, issue_key, weight, is_primary, support_meaning, rationale, source_url) VALUES
    (m_h_amdt_99, 'war_powers', 100, true, 'yea_supports', 'The amendment''s text is the whole question and the question is the authorization itself: it repeals the 2002 authorization for the use of military force against Iraq and the 1991 authorization. war_powers is the subject of who may authorize the use of force and on what standing grant, and this instrument changes that machinery directly rather than ordering any force to move -- so the weight is 100 and the row is primary. war_powers sits in _RD_NO_POLE in stance-helpers.js, so the row is inventory: the reader is told the member voted on a war-powers instrument and is told nothing about a direction, which is the correct outcome for a repeal of superseded standing authority.', 'https://www.congress.gov/amendment/119th-congress/house-amendment/99')
  INSERT INTO vr_measure_issues (measure_id, issue_key, weight, is_primary, support_meaning, rationale, source_url) VALUES
    (m_h_amdt_99, 'restraint', 70, false, 'yea_supports', 'Filed at 70 and secondary, which is the mirror of the face the war-powers resolutions in this same wave carry, and rule 25 requires the reason for the difference to be written down. The resolutions order forces out of an engagement now under way; their operative subject is the scope of American military involvement, so restraint leads there at 100. This amendment moves no forces and ends no engagement -- it withdraws two standing legal authorizations. The restraint reading is real, because a repealed authorization is one fewer basis for future action, but it is a consequence of the change rather than the change, and 70 is where a consequence is recorded.', 'https://www.congress.gov/amendment/119th-congress/house-amendment/99')
