  -- ── roll calls and member votes ───────────────────────────────────────────
  -- The chamber's own document is the vote. Every tally below is the Senate's
  -- <count><yeas>/<nays> block or the clerk's <totals-by-vote> block, counting all 100 or
  -- all 430-437 recorded members — NOT the attributed rows, which are a much smaller set
  -- because the roster admits 221 slugs. There is a specific trap here worth naming: the
  -- LIS <vote_tally> element renders '51-42' as a DISPLAY STRING, which parses to 5142 and
  -- makes the losing side zero, so rule 11 would pass everything. The count block is the
  -- authority and the guards at the end assert the tally against the attributed row count.
  --
  -- Attribution is fail-closed and the two chambers take different paths because the two
  -- sources carry different identifiers. House: the clerk's own name-id, then
  -- db/vr-member-map.json. Senate: there is no bioguide in the LIS XML, so the key is
  -- (surname, state) resolved against the roster with a whole-name compare. A surname that
  -- resolves to more than one distinct person in the same state is SKIPPED and counted,
  -- never guessed — ambiguous skips this wave: 0. Three serving senators are absent from
  -- the roster (Husted OH, Hyde-Smith MS, Armstrong OK) and account for every unresolved
  -- Senate row; that is a roster gap named in the seed, not a reading failure.

  -- senate 119/1 roll 555 · S.J.Res. 83 · On the Motion to Discharge S.J.Res. 83
  --   48-51, 1 not voting · rejected
  --   losing side is 48.485% of the yea+nay pool — rule 11's one-tenth bar is cleared
  --   98 of 100 recorded members resolve to a roster slug; 2 skipped as unmapped
  --   admitted as: exception: discharge
  --   decisiveWhy: A war-powers resolution under 50 U.S.C. 1544(c) reaches the
  --   floor only if the Foreign Relations Committee is discharged, so the
  --   discharge motion IS the vote on the resolution: a rejected motion ends the
  --   measure and no vote on passage ever occurs. This is the same admitted form
  --   F4 used for the arms-sale disapprovals.
  VALUES (m_s_j_res_83, 'senate', 119, 1, 555, DATE '2025-10-08', 'On the Motion to Discharge S.J.Res. 83', 'motion', 'rejected', 'simple',
