  -- H.R. 2056 · border_security w75 PRIMARY yea_supports
  --   The Act's whole mechanism is the state and local end of federal
  --   immigration enforcement: it forbids the District from adopting a law,
  --   policy or practice that stops its entities from sending, receiving,
  --   maintaining or exchanging citizenship or immigration status information,
  --   and from declining lawful federal requests. border_security's written
  --   scope in issue-scope.js names, as what is IN, 'the state and local
  --   cooperation that feeds the federal system' -- this Act is that clause and
  --   almost nothing else. Weight 75 rather than 100 because the key's scope
  --   also covers the physical border and the entry apparatus, which this Act
  --   does not touch, and because the carve-out for witnesses and victims of
  --   crime is a real limit on the mandate rather than a recital. A yea
  --   compelled the cooperation.
  ON CONFLICT (measure_id, issue_key) DO NOTHING;

  -- H.R. 2056 · deportations w70 secondary yea_supports
  --   The second operative limb reaches detainers and release notification --
  --   the District may not decline a lawful request to hold or to notify before
  --   release -- and that is the hand-off by which a person in local custody
  --   enters removal proceedings. deportations' written scope names 'mandatory
  --   custody and removal -- who the executive must detain and place in removal
  --   proceedings'. This Act does not itself order a removal, which is why it is
  --   filed at 70 and secondary: it removes the local discretion that currently
  --   interrupts the chain. The CRS summary confirms the clause; the engrossed
  --   text was read for it rather than the summary alone.
  ON CONFLICT (measure_id, issue_key) DO NOTHING;
  --
  --   DECLINED on H.R. 2056 — tough_on_crime: Refused on the key's own OUT list,
  --   which names 'immigration detention and removal' in terms. The measure
