  --   nothing in tough_on_crime's IN enumeration -- offence elements, offence
  --   levels, mandatory minimums, sentencing enhancements, juvenile adjustment
  --   and expungement -- is engaged. That the bill is about custody is not
  --   enough: the OUT line was written for exactly this confusion.
  --   DECLINED on H.R. 2056 — checks_balances: The Act does constrain what the
  --   District's own government may enact, and that is a federal-local authority
  --   question. Runbook rule 28: checks_balances takes no roll-call mappings.
  --   Named rather than silently dropped, because it is the honest second
  --   reading of the measure and the reason it is not filed is a standing rule,
  --   not an absence.
  --   DECLINED on H.R. 2056 — gov_regulation: Refused as restuffing. F6's
  --   shipped wall forbids using gov_regulation as a home for anything that has
  --   a subject key, and this measure has two.

  -- H.R. 4922 · tough_on_crime w90 PRIMARY yea_supports
  --   Two of the Act's three operative limbs are inside tough_on_crime's written
  --   enumeration verbatim. The key is IN for 'how long a person or a case stays
  --   in the system: offence elements, offence levels, mandatory minimums,
  --   sentencing enhancements, and juvenile adjustment and expungement
  --   eligibility'. Cutting the youth offender ceiling from 24 to 18 is juvenile
  --   adjustment eligibility; repealing the authority to sentence a youth
  --   offender below the mandatory minimum is a mandatory minimum. The key's
  --   pole reads 'Advanced = the vote increased exposure to punishment or time
  --   in custody', and both limbs do that on their face. Weight 90 rather than
  --   100 because the third operative limb -- the Home Rule Act amendment
  --   freezing the Council's sentencing authority -- is a federal-local
  --   authority question this wave refuses to file at all, and the weight is
  --   where that remainder is recorded rather than in a second row on a key that
  --   takes no roll calls.
  ON CONFLICT (measure_id, issue_key) DO NOTHING;
  --
  --   DECLINED on H.R. 4922 — checks_balances: The Home Rule Act limb is a
  --   genuine checks_balances subject: it removes a legislature's power to
  --   legislate in a field. Runbook rule 28 says the key takes no roll-call
  --   mappings, so it is refused on the standing rule and the remainder is
  --   carried in the tough_on_crime weight instead. This is the whole reason
  --   that weight is 90.
  --   DECLINED on H.R. 4922 — justice_reform: Refused, and the reason is
