  --   upward, on the tough_on_crime side of the same pair. Filing both would
  --   double-count one vote across a poled pair.

  -- H.R. 5140 · tough_on_crime w100 PRIMARY yea_supports
  --   One operative provision and nothing else: the age at which a minor charged
  --   with the enumerated violent offences leaves family court for adult court
  --   drops to 14. tough_on_crime's written scope is IN for 'juvenile
  --   adjustment' eligibility by name, and its pole reads 'Advanced = the vote
  --   increased exposure to punishment or time in custody' -- adult court is the
  --   greater exposure, which is the entire point of the change. There is no
  --   remainder to record in a weight, so the weight is 100.
  ON CONFLICT (measure_id, issue_key) DO NOTHING;
  --
  --   DECLINED on H.R. 5140 — justice_reform: Same refusal as on H.R. 4922 and
  --   for the same written reason: the key has no scope note to test against,
  --   and tough_on_crime's OUT list assigns movement in the other direction to
  --   it, which makes these two keys a poled pair rather than two homes for one
