  -- H.R. 5214 · tough_on_crime w90 PRIMARY yea_supports
  --   This one is argued on the key's IN headline and its pole line rather than
  --   on the enumeration, because bail is not in the enumeration and pretending
  --   otherwise would be the keyword reasoning rule 41 forbids. The headline is
  --   'Criminal exposure and time served -- what is an offence, at what level,
  --   and how long a person or a case stays in the system', and the pole is
  --   'Advanced = the vote increased exposure to punishment or time in custody'.
  --   The Act makes detention mandatory for two classes of charge where a judge
  --   now decides, and conditions release on cash for a third. Time in custody
  --   before trial is time in custody, and how long a case stays in the system
  --   is the headline in terms. Weight 90 because the mechanism is pretrial
  --   process rather than an offence level or a sentence, and the enumeration
  --   reaches the latter.
  ON CONFLICT (measure_id, issue_key) DO NOTHING;
  --
  --   DECLINED on H.R. 5214 — justice_reform: As on H.R. 4922 and H.R. 5140: no
