  --   against officers. This Act funds nothing and creates no offence; it moves
  --   a bail decision from a judge to a statute. Adjacency to policing is not
  --   evidence (rule 41).

  -- H.Amdt. 99 · war_powers w100 PRIMARY yea_supports
  --   The amendment's text is the whole question and the question is the
  --   authorization itself: it repeals the 2002 authorization for the use of
  --   military force against Iraq and the 1991 authorization. war_powers is the
  --   subject of who may authorize the use of force and on what standing grant,
  --   and this instrument changes that machinery directly rather than ordering
  --   any force to move -- so the weight is 100 and the row is primary.
  --   war_powers sits in _RD_NO_POLE in stance-helpers.js, so the row is
  --   inventory: the reader is told the member voted on a war-powers instrument
  --   and is told nothing about a direction, which is the correct outcome for a
  --   repeal of superseded standing authority.
  ON CONFLICT (measure_id, issue_key) DO NOTHING;

  -- H.Amdt. 99 · restraint w70 secondary yea_supports
  --   Filed at 70 and secondary, which is the mirror of the face the war-powers
  --   resolutions in this same wave carry, and rule 25 requires the reason for
  --   the difference to be written down. The resolutions order forces out of an
  --   engagement now under way; their operative subject is the scope of American
  --   military involvement, so restraint leads there at 100. This amendment
  --   moves no forces and ends no engagement -- it withdraws two standing legal
  --   authorizations. The restraint reading is real, because a repealed
  --   authorization is one fewer basis for future action, but it is a
  --   consequence of the change rather than the change, and 70 is where a
  --   consequence is recorded.
  ON CONFLICT (measure_id, issue_key) DO NOTHING;
  --
  --   DECLINED on H.Amdt. 99 — strong_defense: Refused, and the argument matters
  --   because the war-powers resolutions in this same wave DO carry
  --   strong_defense at 55 opposed. The reason those carry it is stated in
  --   S.J.Res. 59's own shipped rationale: 'A yea withdraws U.S. forces from an
  --   ongoing engagement absent a vote of Congress.' That sentence is false of
  --   this amendment. Nothing is withdrawn from anywhere; two authorizations
  --   that no operation now relies on are struck from the books, and the
  --   amendment carried 261-167 with support from both sides of the chamber.
  --   Copying the row because the words look alike would be the adjacency
  --   reasoning rule 41 forbids, and it would publish an opposed direction on a
  --   defence key for 261 members on no evidence.
  --   DECLINED on H.Amdt. 99 — foreign_balance: Same written departure as on the
  --   fourteen resolutions: a _balance key is permanently unread by
  --   _rdSuppressedKey(), and F6's wall forbids parking a row there.

  -- ── the seven measures that get no mapping row ─────────────────────────────
  -- Rule 34, and the diff rather than the claim. Each of these seven rolls is
  -- ingested in full and each records no yea or nay that an earlier roll on
  -- the same text does not already record. Withholding the mapping keeps seven
  -- duplicate restraint acts and seven duplicate strong_defense acts per
  -- senator out of the pattern index for one position held once. Nobody's
  -- position is lost: every senator attributed on one of these rolls also
  -- holds a judged position on a roll that keeps its mappings, and the
  -- verification block asserts it.
  --
  -- S.J.Res. 118 · 119/2/58 · 47-53 · new judged pairs: 0
  --     ingested, zero mappings -- member for member identical to roll 46
  --
  -- S.J.Res. 116 · 119/2/69 · 47-53 · new judged pairs: 0
  --     ingested, zero mappings -- member for member identical to roll 46
  --
  -- S.J.Res. 123 · 119/2/79 · 47-52 · new judged pairs: 0
  --     ingested, zero mappings -- the single change is jim_justice to not_voting,
  --     which is not a position
  --
  -- S.J.Res. 114 · 119/2/88 · 46-51 · new judged pairs: 0
  --     ingested, zero mappings -- all four changes are to not_voting (grassley,
  --     mccormick, warner)
  --
  -- S.J.Res. 172 · 119/2/174 · 47-48 · new judged pairs: 0
  --     ingested, zero mappings -- all eight changes are to not_voting
  --
  -- S.J.Res. 180 · 119/2/207 · 47-49 · new judged pairs: 0
  --     ingested, zero mappings -- all eight changes are to not_voting
  --
  -- S.J.Res. 181 · 119/2/216 · 49-50 · new judged pairs: 0
  --     ingested, zero mappings -- three members returned to a position an earlier
  --     roll already records

END $$;

-- ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- VERIFICATION — scoped to THIS WAVE'S 19 rolls and 19 measures.
-- Nothing below counts a session-wide or corpus-wide total. A guard that fails
-- because some other wave landed is a guard that gets deleted, so every count here
-- is taken over the named rolls and the named measures only. The roll ids live in an
-- integer[] local variable rather than a temp table: a data-only migration that sorts
-- after the newest drizzle snapshot may not declare an object, and
-- scripts/test-vr-corrections.mjs reads any CREATE of a TABLE as a declaration
-- regardless of how temporary it is. The element type is the serial vr_rollcalls.id.
-- ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DO $$
DECLARE
  n_measures integer; n_rolls integer; n_votes integer; n_orphan integer; n_issues integer;
  n_badpos integer; n_tally integer; n_hr1069 integer; n_keys integer; n_newkeys integer;
  n_chamber integer; n_rule11 integer;
  n_zero integer; n_orphan_pos integer; n_nokey_primary integer; n_balance integer;
  n_wave_primary_keys integer;
  roll_ids integer[]; mapped_ids integer[]; zero_ids integer[];
BEGIN
  SELECT count(*) INTO n_measures FROM vr_measures
   WHERE congress = 119 AND (measure_type, chamber, number) IN (
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 83'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 90'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 98'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 104'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 118'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 116'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 123'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 114'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 184'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 163'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 185'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 172'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 180'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 181'),
     ('bill','house','H.R. 2056'),
     ('bill','house','H.R. 4922'),
     ('bill','house','H.R. 5140'),
     ('bill','house','H.R. 5214'),
     ('amendment','house','H.Amdt. 99'));
  IF n_measures <> 19 THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Federal wave F7: expected 19 measures on file, found %', n_measures;
  END IF;

  SELECT array_agg(id) INTO roll_ids FROM vr_rollcalls
   WHERE (chamber, congress, session, roll_number) IN (('senate',119,1,555), ('senate',119,1,608), ('senate',119,2,5), ('senate',119,2,46), ('senate',119,2,58), ('senate',119,2,69), ('senate',119,2,79), ('senate',119,2,88), ('senate',119,2,113), ('senate',119,2,118), ('senate',119,2,129), ('senate',119,2,174), ('senate',119,2,207), ('senate',119,2,216), ('house',119,1,171), ('house',119,1,270), ('house',119,1,271), ('house',119,1,298), ('house',119,1,244));
  n_rolls := coalesce(array_length(roll_ids, 1), 0);
  IF n_rolls <> 19 THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Federal wave F7: expected 19 roll calls, found %', n_rolls;
  END IF;

  SELECT count(*) INTO n_votes FROM vr_member_votes WHERE rollcall_id = ANY(roll_ids);
  IF n_votes < 1948 THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Federal wave F7: expected at least 1948 member votes on these rolls, found %', n_votes;
  END IF;

  -- Fail-closed attribution, asserted rather than assumed. A politician_id on one of these
  -- rolls that is not in the roster means the resolver guessed at somebody — the one failure
  -- mode a (surname, state) key can introduce, and the reason ambiguous names are skipped.
  SELECT count(*) INTO n_orphan FROM vr_member_votes v
   WHERE v.rollcall_id = ANY(roll_ids)
     AND v.politician_id NOT IN ('adam_smith', 'adrian_smith', 'aguilar', 'alsobrooks', 'andy_harris', 'andy_kim', 'angie_craig', 'angus_king', 'aoc', 'arrington', 'ashley_moody', 'ayanna_pressley', 'banks', 'barrasso', 'bennet', 'bennie_thompson', 'blackburn', 'blumenthal', 'blunt_rochester', 'bmoore', 'boebert', 'booker', 'boozman', 'brendan_boyle', 'brian_babin', 'brian_mast', 'britt', 'bruce_westerman', 'bryan_steil', 'cantwell', 'capito', 'cassidy', 'chellie_pingree', 'chip_roy', 'chris_murphy', 'clyburn', 'collins', 'comer', 'coons', 'cortez_masto', 'cotton', 'crapo', 'crockett', 'cruz', 'curtis', 'daines', 'dan_crenshaw', 'dan_goldman', 'dan_sullivan', 'deb_fischer', 'debbie_dingell', 'delauro', 'delia_ramirez', 'diana_degette', 'dina_titus', 'don_bacon', 'don_davis', 'donalds', 'duckworth', 'durbin', 'emmer', 'ernst', 'fetterman', 'fitzpatrick', 'foxx', 'frank_lucas', 'french_hill', 'gabe_vasquez', 'gallego', 'garbarino', 'gillibrand', 'glenn_thompson', 'graham', 'grassley', 'greg_landsman', 'guthrie', 'hagerty', 'haley_stevens', 'hawley', 'heinrich', 'hickenlooper', 'hirono', 'hoeven', 'jake_auchincloss', 'jan_schakowsky', 'jared_golden', 'jared_huffman', 'jason_smith', 'jayapal', 'jeffries', 'jerry_moran', 'jim_himes', 'jim_jordan', 'jim_justice', 'jim_mcgovern', 'john_cornyn', 'jon_ossoff', 'josh_brecheen', 'josh_gottheimer', 'julie_fedorchak', 'kaine', 'kclark', 'kennedy', 'kennedy_john', 'kevin_cramer', 'kevin_hern', 'khanna', 'klobuchar', 'lankford', 'lee', 'lujan', 'lummis', 'luna', 'maggie_hassan', 'maloy', 'mariannette_miller_meeks', 'marie_gluesenkamp_perez', 'mark_kelly', 'markey', 'massie', 'maxine_waters', 'maxwell_frost', 'mcclain', 'mcconnell', 'mccormick', 'meeks', 'melanie_stansbury', 'merkley', 'michael_guest', 'mike_bost', 'mike_collins', 'mike_ezell', 'mike_flood', 'mike_johnson', 'mike_lawler', 'mike_rounds', 'mike_simpson', 'moreno', 'mtg', 'mullin', 'murkowski', 'murray', 'nadler', 'nancy_mace', 'neal', 'neguse', 'omar', 'owens', 'padilla', 'pallone', 'peters', 'raja_krishnamoorthi', 'rand_paul', 'raskin', 'reed', 'rick_crawford', 'rick_larsen', 'rick_scott', 'ricketts', 'risch', 'rob_bresnahan', 'robert_garcia', 'roger_marshall', 'roger_williams', 'ron_johnson', 'rosen', 'russ_fulcher', 'ryan_mackenzie', 'sam_graves', 'sanders', 'sarah_mcbride', 'scalise', 'schatz', 'schiff', 'schmitt', 'schumer', 'scott_perry', 'seth_moulton', 'shaheen', 'sheehy', 'slotkin', 'stefanik', 'steny_hoyer', 'stephanie_bice', 'steve_womack', 'summer_lee', 'susie_lee', 'takano', 'tammy_baldwin', 'ted_budd', 'ted_lieu', 'teresa_leger_fernandez', 'thune', 'tillis', 'tim_scott', 'tina_smith', 'tlaib', 'todd_young', 'tom_cole', 'tom_suozzi', 'tommy_tuberville', 'torres', 'trent_kelly', 'troy_downing', 'van_hollen', 'walberg', 'warner', 'warnock', 'warren', 'welch', 'whitehouse', 'wicker', 'wyden', 'zach_nunn', 'zoe_lofgren');
  IF n_orphan > 0 THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Federal wave F7: % member vote(s) on these rolls carry a politician_id outside db/vr-member-map.json. Attribution here is fail-closed, so this is a bug, not a roster gap.', n_orphan;
  END IF;

  SELECT count(*) INTO n_badpos FROM vr_member_votes
   WHERE rollcall_id = ANY(roll_ids) AND position NOT IN ('yea','nay','present','not_voting');
  IF n_badpos > 0 THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Federal wave F7: % member vote(s) carry a position outside the closed vocabulary.', n_badpos;
  END IF;

  -- The tally is the chamber's, not the roster's. Two separate things can go wrong here and
  -- they need two separate guards, because the obvious single guard is wrong: on two of these
  -- rolls (119/2/174 at 95-0 with 5 not voting, 119/2/207 at 96-0 with 4) the yea+nay pool is
  -- SMALLER than the attributed row count, since attributed rows include the not_voting
  -- positions of members who are in the roster. So the subset check compares the pool against
  -- the attributed rows that carry a JUDGED position, which genuinely is a subset of it.
  SELECT count(*) INTO n_tally FROM vr_rollcalls r
   WHERE r.id = ANY(roll_ids)
     AND (r.totals->>'yea')::int + (r.totals->>'nay')::int
         < (SELECT count(*) FROM vr_member_votes v WHERE v.rollcall_id = r.id
             AND v.position IN ('yea','nay'));
  IF n_tally > 0 THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Federal wave F7: % roll(s) have a yea+nay pool smaller than the number of attributed yea/nay rows. The attributed set is a subset of the chamber, so this means the totals were recomputed from the rows.', n_tally;
  END IF;

  -- And the check that actually catches a roster-derived total, which is the failure worth
  -- fearing: it would publish a vote that did not happen, with a plausible-looking margin.
  -- Every Senate roll here sums to exactly 100 across yea, nay, present and not voting, and
  -- every House roll to between 400 and 440. The roster admits 98 senators and 117
  -- representatives, so a total assembled from the rows fails both bounds immediately.
  SELECT count(*) INTO n_chamber FROM vr_rollcalls r
   WHERE r.id = ANY(roll_ids)
     AND ((r.chamber = 'senate' AND (r.totals->>'yea')::int + (r.totals->>'nay')::int
            + (r.totals->>'present')::int + (r.totals->>'notVoting')::int <> 100)
       OR (r.chamber = 'house' AND ((r.totals->>'yea')::int + (r.totals->>'nay')::int
            + (r.totals->>'present')::int + (r.totals->>'notVoting')::int NOT BETWEEN 400 AND 440)));
  IF n_chamber > 0 THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Federal wave F7: % roll(s) do not account for a full chamber. A Senate roll totals 100 and a House roll 400-440; anything near 98 or 117 is the roster subset masquerading as the chamber.', n_chamber;
  END IF;

  -- Rule 11, in the migration and not only in the harness, because the specific bug it
  -- catches lives in the ingest path this migration was generated from. The LIS XML carries a
  -- <vote_tally> element that renders '51-42' as a DISPLAY STRING; read as a number it is
  -- 5142, which makes the losing side zero and every roll look unanimous-but-contested. The
  -- authority is the <count><yeas>/<nays> block, and if that substitution ever happens again
  -- the losing share collapses and this guard fires instead of the site publishing it.
  SELECT count(*) INTO n_rule11 FROM vr_rollcalls r
   WHERE r.id = ANY(roll_ids)
     AND 10 * least((r.totals->>'yea')::int, (r.totals->>'nay')::int)
         < (r.totals->>'yea')::int + (r.totals->>'nay')::int;
  IF n_rule11 > 0 THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Federal wave F7: % roll(s) fail rule 11 — the losing side is under a tenth of the yea+nay pool, so the question was not contested. Observed range this wave: 39.019%% to 49.495%%.', n_rule11;
  END IF;

  SELECT count(*) INTO n_issues FROM vr_measure_issues
   WHERE measure_id IN (SELECT id FROM vr_measures WHERE congress = 119
     AND (measure_type, chamber, number) IN (
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 83'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 90'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 98'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 104'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 118'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 116'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 123'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 114'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 184'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 163'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 185'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 172'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 180'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 181'),
     ('bill','house','H.R. 2056'),
     ('bill','house','H.R. 4922'),
     ('bill','house','H.R. 5140'),
     ('bill','house','H.R. 5214'),
     ('amendment','house','H.Amdt. 99')));
  IF n_issues <> 28 THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Federal wave F7: expected exactly 28 issue mappings on this wave''s measures, found %. A higher count means somebody added a row to feed coverage or reopened one of the seven rule 34 measures; the seed refuses 31 keys on these measures in writing.', n_issues;
  END IF;

  -- Rule 34's decision, asserted as a number. Exactly seven of this wave's measures carry
  -- no issue row, and the seed carries the member-for-member diff for each. If this count
  -- drops, somebody mapped a duplicate roll and inflated every senator's restraint depth.
  SELECT count(*) INTO n_zero FROM vr_measures m
   WHERE m.congress = 119
     AND (m.measure_type, m.chamber, m.number) IN (
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 83'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 90'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 98'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 104'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 118'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 116'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 123'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 114'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 184'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 163'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 185'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 172'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 180'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 181'),
     ('bill','house','H.R. 2056'),
     ('bill','house','H.R. 4922'),
     ('bill','house','H.R. 5140'),
     ('bill','house','H.R. 5214'),
     ('amendment','house','H.Amdt. 99'))
     AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM vr_measure_issues i WHERE i.measure_id = m.id);
  IF n_zero <> 7 THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Federal wave F7: expected exactly 7 measures with no issue row (runbook rule 34, argued in the seed under censusRule34), found %.', n_zero;
  END IF;

  -- The check that makes rule 34 admissible here, and the only one that could fail for a
  -- reason that matters: no senator's judged position may live ONLY on a zero-mapping roll.
  -- Withholding a mapping is honest when the roll records nothing new and dishonest the
  -- moment it is the sole record of somebody's yea or nay.
  SELECT array_agg(id) INTO mapped_ids FROM vr_rollcalls
   WHERE (chamber, congress, session, roll_number) IN (('senate',119,1,555), ('senate',119,1,608), ('senate',119,2,5), ('senate',119,2,46), ('senate',119,2,113), ('senate',119,2,118), ('senate',119,2,129), ('house',119,1,171), ('house',119,1,270), ('house',119,1,271), ('house',119,1,298), ('house',119,1,244));
  SELECT array_agg(id) INTO zero_ids FROM vr_rollcalls
   WHERE (chamber, congress, session, roll_number) IN (('senate',119,2,58), ('senate',119,2,69), ('senate',119,2,79), ('senate',119,2,88), ('senate',119,2,174), ('senate',119,2,207), ('senate',119,2,216));
  SELECT count(*) INTO n_orphan_pos FROM (
    SELECT DISTINCT v.politician_id FROM vr_member_votes v
     WHERE v.rollcall_id = ANY(zero_ids) AND v.position IN ('yea','nay')
       AND NOT EXISTS (
         SELECT 1 FROM vr_member_votes w
          WHERE w.rollcall_id = ANY(mapped_ids) AND w.politician_id = v.politician_id
            AND w.position IN ('yea','nay'))
  ) t;
  IF n_orphan_pos > 0 THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Federal wave F7: % member(s) hold a judged position only on a roll this wave leaves unmapped. Rule 34 admits a duplicate when it is the only record of somebody''s position, so either those rolls must be mapped or this wave is hiding a vote.', n_orphan_pos;
  END IF;

  -- No new vocabulary. Every key used here must already appear on a measure outside this
  -- wave, which is the strongest available assertion that nothing was invented.
  SELECT count(DISTINCT issue_key) INTO n_keys FROM vr_measure_issues
   WHERE measure_id IN (SELECT id FROM vr_measures WHERE congress = 119
     AND (measure_type, chamber, number) IN (
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 83'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 90'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 98'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 104'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 118'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 116'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 123'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 114'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 184'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 163'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 185'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 172'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 180'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 181'),
     ('bill','house','H.R. 2056'),
     ('bill','house','H.R. 4922'),
     ('bill','house','H.R. 5140'),
     ('bill','house','H.R. 5214'),
     ('amendment','house','H.Amdt. 99')));
  IF n_keys <> 6 THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Federal wave F7: this wave writes % distinct keys, expected 6 (border_security, deportations, restraint, strong_defense, tough_on_crime, war_powers).', n_keys;
  END IF;
  SELECT count(*) INTO n_newkeys FROM (
    SELECT DISTINCT i.issue_key FROM vr_measure_issues i
     WHERE i.measure_id IN (SELECT id FROM vr_measures WHERE congress = 119
       AND (measure_type, chamber, number) IN (
       ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 83'),
       ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 90'),
       ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 98'),
       ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 104'),
       ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 184'),
       ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 163'),
       ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 185'),
       ('bill','house','H.R. 2056'),
       ('bill','house','H.R. 4922'),
       ('bill','house','H.R. 5140'),
       ('bill','house','H.R. 5214'),
       ('amendment','house','H.Amdt. 99')))
       AND NOT EXISTS (
         SELECT 1 FROM vr_measure_issues j WHERE j.issue_key = i.issue_key
          AND j.measure_id NOT IN (SELECT id FROM vr_measures WHERE congress = 119
            AND (measure_type, chamber, number) IN (
            ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 83'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 90'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 98'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 104'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 118'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 116'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 123'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 114'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 184'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 163'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 185'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 172'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 180'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 181'),
     ('bill','house','H.R. 2056'),
     ('bill','house','H.R. 4922'),
     ('bill','house','H.R. 5140'),
     ('bill','house','H.R. 5214'),
     ('amendment','house','H.Amdt. 99'))))
  ) t;
  IF n_newkeys > 0 THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Federal wave F7: % key(s) exist only on this wave''s measures. This wave adds NO vocabulary — the two gaps it found, arms transfers to a partner other than Israel and police accountability rules, are named and left open in the seed — so a key with no prior instrument means one was invented here.', n_newkeys;
  END IF;

  -- The _balance wall, asserted where it can be. F6's shipped wall forbids parking a row on
  -- a key _rdSuppressedKey() leaves permanently unread, and this wave's one written
  -- departure from the S.J.Res. 59 face is exactly that refusal.
  SELECT count(*) INTO n_balance FROM vr_measure_issues
   WHERE measure_id IN (SELECT id FROM vr_measures WHERE congress = 119
     AND (measure_type, chamber, number) IN (
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 83'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 90'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 98'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 104'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 118'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 116'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 123'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 114'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 184'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 163'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 185'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 172'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 180'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 181'),
     ('bill','house','H.R. 2056'),
     ('bill','house','H.R. 4922'),
     ('bill','house','H.R. 5140'),
     ('bill','house','H.R. 5214'),
     ('amendment','house','H.Amdt. 99')))
     AND issue_key LIKE '%\_balance';
  IF n_balance > 0 THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Federal wave F7: % row(s) on this wave''s measures sit on a *_balance key. Those rows are permanently unread and F6''s wall forbids using them as a car park.', n_balance;
  END IF;

  -- Rule 30's wall, in the two forms that are actually true. First: every key this wave
  -- writes must carry at least one primary row SOMEWHERE in the corpus, this wave included.
  -- A key with no primary anywhere would mean every reading on it prints _rdPackageNote's
  -- sentence, and that is a hundred readings changed by a row-level choice.
  SELECT count(*) INTO n_nokey_primary FROM (
    SELECT i.issue_key FROM vr_measure_issues i
     WHERE i.issue_key IN ('border_security', 'deportations', 'restraint', 'strong_defense', 'tough_on_crime', 'war_powers')
     GROUP BY i.issue_key
    HAVING count(*) FILTER (WHERE i.is_primary) = 0
  ) t;
  IF n_nokey_primary > 0 THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Federal wave F7: % of the keys this wave writes carry no primary row anywhere in the corpus. Rule 30: every reading on such a key prints the package sentence, so the primary wall is checked before a depth pass, not after.', n_nokey_primary;
  END IF;

  -- Second: the split itself, asserted as a set. This wave supplies a primary on exactly
  -- 4 of its 6 keys (border_security, restraint, tough_on_crime, war_powers) and secondaries only on
  -- deportations and strong_defense. That is a decision with a written reason in the seed under
  -- readDisclosure.primaryWallPerKey, and it was measured: zero members become newly readable
  -- on a secondary-only key and zero readings start printing the package sentence. If somebody
  -- later flips one of this wave's primaries to a secondary, that measurement is void, so the
  -- set is pinned here rather than left to be re-derived by whoever is looking.
  SELECT count(*) INTO n_wave_primary_keys FROM (
    SELECT i.issue_key FROM vr_measure_issues i
     WHERE i.measure_id IN (SELECT id FROM vr_measures WHERE congress = 119
       AND (measure_type, chamber, number) IN (
       ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 83'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 90'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 98'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 104'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 118'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 116'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 123'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 114'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 184'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 163'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 185'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 172'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 180'),
     ('resolution','senate','S.J.Res. 181'),
     ('bill','house','H.R. 2056'),
     ('bill','house','H.R. 4922'),
     ('bill','house','H.R. 5140'),
     ('bill','house','H.R. 5214'),
     ('amendment','house','H.Amdt. 99')))
       AND i.is_primary
       AND i.issue_key IN ('border_security', 'restraint', 'tough_on_crime', 'war_powers')
     GROUP BY i.issue_key
  ) t;
  IF n_wave_primary_keys <> 4 THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Federal wave F7: this wave supplies a primary row on % of its keys, expected 4 (border_security, restraint, tough_on_crime, war_powers).', n_wave_primary_keys;
  END IF;

  -- The standing refusal, re-asserted where it can actually be checked.
  SELECT count(*) INTO n_hr1069 FROM vr_measure_issues
   WHERE measure_id IN (SELECT id FROM vr_measures WHERE congress = 119 AND number IN ('H.R. 1069','H.R. 973'));
  IF n_hr1069 > 0 THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Federal wave F7: H.R. 1069 / H.R. 973 now carry % issue row(s). Both are deliberately unmapped — F1 argued and refused the public_schools row, and rule 3 refuses gov_regulation on H.R. 973. F7 writes no new key, so nothing in it reopens either.', n_hr1069;
  END IF;

  RAISE NOTICE 'Federal wave F7 verified: % measures (% with no issue row, rule 34), % rolls, % member votes, % issue rows on % keys.', n_measures, n_zero, n_rolls, n_votes, n_issues, n_keys;
END $$;
